{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3460","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3460","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3460\",\"parent_revision\":\"0789d8176edc932672146a03babbc95ebf7616d24f549209f6b6cdc12dd4cccd\",\"root_revision\":\"0789d8176edc932672146a03babbc95ebf7616d24f549209f6b6cdc12dd4cccd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe plan and task graph encodes several relationship kinds as node attributes rather than typed edges:\\n\\n| in `sam_schema/core/models.py` | what it actually is | consumed by logic? |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `dependencies` | CONTROL | yes |\\n| `conflict_group` | STATE \u2014 mutual exclusion over a shared resource | yes |\\n| `is_bookend` / `bookend_type` | EVIDENCE \u2014 T0 establishes the baseline TN checks against | yes |\\n| `blocked_by` | unclear | **no** \u2014 read only by models, writers, backends, `cli_inputs` |\\n| `parallelize_with` | unclear | **no** \u2014 same |\\n\\nEstablished by grep across `dh_core`, `sam_schema` and `backlog_core`, excluding tests: neither `blocked_by` nor `parallelize_with` reaches any decision. They are carried in every task record, serialized to every backend, and decide nothing.\\n\\nAUTHORITY, DATA, ERROR, RECOVERY and INVALIDATES have no representation at all.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What That Cost Concretely\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo defects fixed separately on `worktree-melodic-plotting-emerson` are the same defect:\\n\\n- `import` marked a task with status `complete` as `accepted`. `complete` is the runner's claim; `accepted` is the judge's verdict, and only `accepted` satisfies a dependent. Same column, different authority.\\n- `update --set status=complete` moved a task to complete as a data write \u2014 no lease check, no report check, no cascade, no `task.state` event.\\n\\nBoth are authority violations. Nothing could check authority because nothing modelled it. Two more of the same shape: the TN send-back's `FILES_CHANGED` overlap is prose because there is no DATA edge, and `from-milestone --replace` deleted rows no event accounted for because there is no INVALIDATES edge.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Decision\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRecorded in `ADR-{this issue}-1`. Scenario **C first, then A when C is functional**:\\n\\n- **C** \u2014 the IR owns the six edge types that have no home today (AUTHORITY, EVIDENCE, DATA, ERROR, RECOVERY, INVALIDATES), inside the work ledger. CONTROL keeps flowing from `dependencies` and STATE from `conflict_group`. No backend, MCP schema, skill file or record migration moves.\\n- **A** \u2014 the IR becomes the domain model; `Task`/`Plan` become a serialization view. Measured blast radius: 71 files importing the models, 7 `TaskBackend` implementations across 10 backend modules, 3 MCP tools, 44 skill and agent files naming a task field.\\n\\nC's stated risk is that its dual-home period (CONTROL on the node, other edges on edges) becomes permanent. The ADR carries the exit criteria that trigger A.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Governing Contract\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-ir/ASSESSOR-CONTRACT.md` \u2014 the eight edge types, the node record, the falsified predicates, the `BROKEN` / `CONTRACT_UNSPECIFIED` / `AMBIGUOUS` severity rule, the projections, and the three-part validation of any report produced from the graph.\\n</div>\\n\\n## First Deliverable\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe schema plus a falsification that re-derives the four defects above and shows each is either unrepresentable or mechanically detectable. A defect the IR can neither refuse nor detect is the result that says the design does not earn its cost.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"41624e466d5058583e9ee053384b6a58328471f22f4415af40e2648daf8110c4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyivg\"}"}